  "scope": "Exact coefficient-algebra computations at twelve sites: the replica-swap unit C0 and transposition class sum T generate a five-dimensional commutative subalgebra, with T satisfying x(x-1)^2(x+1)^2. The eight primitive central idempotents see eigenvalues 0,1,4, with the two dual blocks carrying nontrivial nilpotent actions. The coefficient combination C3+C5 completes the full ten-dimensional algebra and, together with T, separates the eight central idempotents at the character level; this is a coefficient-algebra statement, not a split of the cut module coarse blocks. This is not the eight-dimensional R,T orbit on the cut module; no cut-module rank, two-cut pairing, rank bound, or factoring score change is claimed.",
